        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;ketigid&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"ketigid\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My guess would either be damage is dealt by The Matriarch (as she is always guarenteed to be an available target), or the damage comes from nothing, like a good deal of environment cards from the core set.  Though, in general, it appears that damage listed on villain cards tend to come from villain targets.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I beg to differ on this. To my best knowledge, nearly all damage dealt by the core environments states “This card deals”, so it is clear who/what the source of the damage is. Sometimes, it is from a target, such as the T-rex. Sometimes, it is from a non-target, such as Volcanic Eruption.</p>\n<p>The only exception I’m aware of is Kraken, which says “At the end of the environment turn, deal the non-environment target with the lowest hp 5 melee damage.” For Kraken, I believe it should say “this card” as well but was mistakenly left out. If it is indeed a typo, someone should quickly inform GtG to add that to the 2nd edition before sending for printing!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><em>cough</em> I think a little fairy may have gotten your message across.</p>",
